 { By moving his king in V-form, White manages to capture the a7-pawn without letting the black king reach the key square on c7. } 1. { -KEY- } Ke6 $1 ( { Not } 1. Ke7 $2 Kc3 $1 2. Kd7 Kd4 $1 ( { avoiding } 2. Ke6 Kc4 $2 3. Kc6 $1 { with obstruction } ) 
3. Kc6 Ke5 4. Kb7 Kd6 5. Kxa7 Kc7 { and Black reaches his goal. } ) 
Kc3 2. Kd5 $1 { Obstruction while approaching the queenside. } Kd3 ( { Equally useless is } 2... Kb4 3. Kc6 Ka5 4. Kb7 { etc. } ) 
3. Kc6 Ke4 4. Kb7 Kd5 5. Kxa7 Kc6 6. Kb8 { White wins. The diagonal route (f7-e6-d5-c6-b7) is geometrically longer than the straight route (f7-e7-d7-c7-b7), but in both cases it takes the white king four moves to reach b7. } 
