 { How should White cope with the enemy a-pawn while keeping his kingside pawns intact? } 1. { -KEY- } Ke1 $1 { The right route, in order to keep the e-pawn mobile. } ( { The more natural } 1. Ke3 $2 { permits } Kf6 $1 2. Kd4 Kg5 3. e4 Kxg4 4. e5 Kg5 5. Kd5 a4 6. e6 a3 7. e7 a2 8. e8=Q $11 a1=Q $11 { with excellent drawing chances - Pozharsky. } ) 
Kf6 2. e4 $1 Ke5 ( { Or } 2... Kg5 3. e5 { with similar play. } ) 
3. g5 ( { Now that the e- and g-pawns defend themselves mutually, White wins easily by picking up the a-pawn; e.g. } 3. g5 a4 4. Kd2 a3 5. Kc3 { etc. } ) 

